  "annotation": {
    "schema_version": 5,
    "type": "bugfix",
    "problem": [
      {
        "text": "The minimal generation example appended the sampler's device-resident result directly to the tokenized context. With CPU context and CUDA sampling, that concatenation crosses devices.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_a3548486e98a4b619654f1919346f5ff",
          "call_88109a0a53e94d5f947057053b95757d",
          "call_4b5cd173ce5d455188c6679d39e80538"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "reasoning": [
      {
        "text": "Moving the sampled token to CPU at the append boundary preserves host-side context management without changing where model inference or sampling runs.",
        "basis": "inference",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6e5923199e46465caefccd8c17ccf138",
          "call_733f6e5e6862439790df08bdad884bf3",
          "call_0b8c1a71ea574a99a97b325b8ea808f3"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "impact": [
      {
        "text": "Only the example changes: concatenation now uses sample.cpu(), and the hardcoded model directory switches from eval_models/.../2.0bpw to models/.../4.0bpw. The directory labels do not establish the contents or quality of those local artifacts.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_6e5923199e46465caefccd8c17ccf138"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "source_notes": [
      {
        "text": "Issue #7, \u201cquantizing model: undefined symbol: __cxa_call_terminate,\u201d reports an extension import failure; issue #15, \u201c`cogito-v1-preview-qwen-32B` generates incoherent output for bpw <= 2.5,\u201d reports quantization-quality problems. Neither discussion identifies this example's token-concatenation change.",
        "basis": "source",
        "evidence": [
          "call_9476092102104188aaf2a020d2faeb44",
          "call_30719b25dad94e7eb949665a815cf83b"
        ]
      }
    ],
    "limitations": [
      "No model inference or CUDA execution was performed; device-transfer correctness and runtime cost were assessed from source only.",
      "A standard-library scalar computation cannot meaningfully validate PyTorch device placement or concatenation, so no substitute arithmetic test was run.",
      "The hardcoded replacement model directory's availability and contents remain unverified."
    ],
    "links": [
      "543c4b27714c6a677a6e714c452d62532f634cff"
    ],
    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "usage-evaluation",
        "title": "Keep generation context on CPU",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Tokenizer.encode constructs the single-string token tensor without an explicit device. DefaultSampler uses temperature, top-p filtering and sampling; its sampling implementation operates on the logits' device and reshapes the result to the logits' leading dimensions without transferring it to CPU.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_88109a0a53e94d5f947057053b95757d",
              "call_af8d8ea2be7a4a4eac7e542576e07d51",
              "call_4b5cd173ce5d455188c6679d39e80538"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The fix transfers only a non-stop sampled token before appending it along the sequence dimension. Stop-token detection still happens first. The appended token becomes the next iteration's input, while context length continues to determine past_len.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_6e5923199e46465caefccd8c17ccf138",
              "call_a3548486e98a4b619654f1919346f5ff"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Keeping context on CPU fits the existing model interface: Model.forward passes each intermediate through prepare_for_device, which moves it to the receiving module's device when necessary. The patch therefore fixes the application-side append rather than changing the sampler's return-device contract.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_733f6e5e6862439790df08bdad884bf3",
              "call_0b8c1a71ea574a99a97b325b8ea808f3",
              "call_6e5923199e46465caefccd8c17ccf138"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The earlier entry describes this script as a low-level cached generation example and identifies the built-in generator as the higher-level alternative. This change retains that educational structure.",
            "basis": "ancestor",
            "evidence": [
              "call_7ed81a707cd9487a93c41b2bf0a3f9f6"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Fixes the minimal generation example's device boundary by copying sampled tokens to CPU before appending them, and updates its hardcoded model path."
  },
